Rule 1 (lambd must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must have a floating-point dtype: 6–8 for float16/float32/float64; avoids 'Char' int8)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 3 (input must be a tensor argument; rules out passing a Python/NumPy number)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (well-defined tensor shape: all dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : 0 ≤ shape(v_1, i)
